{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2189-07-17 23:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having abdominal pain and nausea again. Can you tell me what’s been going on since your last discharge?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2189-07-17 23:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, since I got home, I’ve had constant nausea, barely eating, and lost about 10 pounds. I wasn’t passing gas or having bowel movements, and the pain got worse. I went to the ER and they said it was another blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2189-07-17 23:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And they placed a nasogastric tube for decompression. We’ll keep that in for now to help rest your bowel. You’re on IV fluids and TPN for nutrition, given your history."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2189-07-17 23:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I ever be able to eat again? I’m so tired of not being able to keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2189-07-17 23:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re hoping to find a long-term solution. Right now, your bowel isn’t moving properly due to your sclerosing mesenteritis and past surgeries. We’ll focus on managing this without surgery, since that’s not likely to help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2189-07-18 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show mild anemia and your liver enzymes are a bit elevated, but stable. We’re continuing your TPN through the femoral line for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2189-07-18 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the TPN helping? I still feel weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2189-07-18 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s supporting your nutrition, but it takes time. We’re increasing the volume to help with hydration too. We’ll monitor your response over the next few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2189-07-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a small bowel follow-through with contrast. The dye moves slowly through the upper jejunum but eventually reaches the colon. There’s no clear blockage point, which suggests a functional obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2189-07-20 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a physical blockage? What does that mean for treatment?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2189-07-20 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s more about the bowel not moving properly. Surgery isn’t recommended given your history. We’re considering a G-tube for long-term decompression so you can manage symptoms at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2189-07-20 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A feeding tube again? I had one before, but it was removed. Will this help with the bloating and nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2189-07-20 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, this one will be used mainly to vent the stomach and reduce pressure. You’ll also get water flushes through it to stay hydrated. It’s meant to improve your comfort and prevent repeated hospitalizations."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2189-07-25 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve scheduled a push enteroscopy to look directly at the jejunum. It may help us see if there are any areas we can treat, though we don’t expect to find a stricture."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2189-07-25 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt? And what happens if they don’t find anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2189-07-25 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be sedated, so it won’t be painful. If no treatable narrowing is found, we’ll proceed with the G-tube plan. That’s still the best option for long-term management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2189-07-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The enteroscopy showed dilated jejunum with some sharp turns, but no areas narrow enough to dilate. No intervention was done. We’re moving forward with G-tube placement tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2189-07-27 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m nervous, but I trust you. Will I be able to go home soon after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2189-07-27 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll wait 24 hours before using the tube. Once you’re stable and we confirm it’s working, we’ll start planning your discharge with home TPN and care instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2189-07-28 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The G-tube was placed successfully. It’s not to be used for 24 hours. We’ll start with water flushes and venting after that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2189-07-28 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel a little sore, but okay. When can I start sipping water?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2189-07-28 13:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll allow small sips of clear liquids every 8 hours once we start using the tube. You’ll need to watch for increased bloating or pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2189-07-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. The G-tube is draining bilious fluid, which is expected. We’ve started 150cc water flushes every 8 hours through the tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2189-07-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I passed a little gas yesterday. Is that a good sign?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2189-07-29 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s a positive sign of some return of bowel function, even if slow. We’re not expecting full recovery, but every bit helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2189-07-29 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Doctor, I’m having trouble finding the right words. And my right arm feels weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2189-07-29 20:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ll order a CT head right away to make sure there’s no new stroke. You have a history of stroke, so we need to be cautious."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2189-07-29 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT shows no new bleeding or stroke. It’s consistent with your old left caudate infarct. We’ll get neurology to evaluate you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2189-07-29 22:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not a new stroke? But why am I having trouble speaking now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2189-07-29 22:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be related to your prior brain injury. Neurology will help determine if it’s a new issue or part of your baseline. They may recommend an EEG."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2189-07-30 06:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Neurology saw you. They recommend an EEG and a CTA of the head and neck to check your blood vessels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2189-07-30 06:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Do I need another IV? My veins are so hard to access."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2189-07-30 06:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll place a midline in your arm to give the contrast for the CTA. It’s less invasive than a PICC and should work for this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2189-07-30 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The midline was placed successfully. The CTA is scheduled for later today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2189-07-30 18:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news. The CTA shows no new blockages in your brain vessels. Your carotids are normal. The speech issues are likely related to your old stroke. Neurology recommends follow-up with your neurologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2189-07-30 18:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad it’s not another stroke. My arm feels better already. The word-finding is still hard, but it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2189-07-30 18:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s encouraging. We’ll continue to monitor. The midline will be removed before you go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2189-07-31 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re increasing your TPN volume to help with hydration. You’re also doing well with the water flushes through the G-tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2189-07-31 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I take my pain meds by mouth now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2189-07-31 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but you’ll need to clamp the G-tube for an hour after. We’re switching you to Dilaudid suppositories for severe pain—they worked well and avoid stomach irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2189-08-01 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your hemoglobin has dropped a bit, but it’s expected with your chronic anemia. We’re not transfusing—you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2189-08-01 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m always tired. Is there anything else we can do?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2189-08-01 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re optimizing your nutrition and hydration. The anemia is chronic, tied to your other conditions. We’ll monitor it with weekly labs at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2189-08-02 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re making progress. You’re tolerating sips, the G-tube is working, and your pain is controlled. We’re planning for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2189-08-02 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What will I need to do at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2189-08-02 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get TPN nightly, 150cc water flushes every 8 hours through the G-tube, and take meds as prescribed. Limit clear liquids to a few sips every 8 hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2189-08-02 08:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my blood thinner? I was on Xarelto."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2189-08-02 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re switching you to Lovenox injections twice daily. Because of your bowel issues, we’re concerned you might not absorb oral meds well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2189-08-02 08:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need to give myself shots? I’m nervous about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2189-08-02 08:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "A nurse will teach you and your husband how. It’s a small needle, under the skin. You’ll get pre-filled syringes. You’ll do fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2189-08-03 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared for discharge tomorrow. You have an appointment with your new GI surgeon in a few days to coordinate your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2189-08-03 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will they help me find a primary doctor and neurologist too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2189-08-03 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’ll help coordinate all your specialists. You’ll also follow up with pain management for your Dilaudid prescription."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2189-08-03 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What if my belly swells up or I start vomiting again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2189-08-03 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call your doctor or go to the ER if you have increasing pain, distension, or can’t keep liquids down. Those could be signs the obstruction is worsening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2189-08-03 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pharmacy will fill your Dilaudid suppositories tonight. Bring both prescriptions—one for 12 and one for 60."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2189-08-03 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the G-tube care—any special instructions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2189-08-03 14:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep the site clean and dry. Rotate the tube daily. Call if there’s redness, swelling, or leakage around it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re officially discharged. We’ll send all your records to your new team. Take care, and follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee. I’m ready to go home and start feeling better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been through a lot. We’re confident this plan will help you manage your symptoms. Call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And thank you for explaining everything so clearly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Take it one day at a time. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best. Goodbye for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye. Travel safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care of yourself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll be in touch with your new team to ensure a smooth transition."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s reassuring. I appreciate all the coordination."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s important you have support. Don’t hesitate to reach out if you have questions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. Thank you for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. Wishing you a smooth recovery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Me too. Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:54:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2189-08-04 07:57:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m looking forward to it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2189-08-04 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re glad we could help. See you soon in follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2189-08-04 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll be there. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2189-08-04 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2189-08-04 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2189-08-04 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye. Rest well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2189-08-04 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2189-08-04 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re very welcome. We’re rooting for you."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2189-07-17 23:05:00",
    "admission_end": "2189-08-04 17:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a complex history of sclerosing mesenteritis, chronic small bowel obstructions, and prior abdominal surgeries was readmitted for recurrent abdominal pain, nausea, and failure to pass flatus, consistent with a functional small bowel obstruction. She was managed conservatively with bowel rest, NG tube decompression, and TPN. After no improvement over the first week, a small bowel follow-through and push enteroscopy showed slow transit without a transition point, confirming a functional obstruction. A G-tube was placed for long-term decompression and hydration via free water flushes. During her stay, she developed transient word-finding difficulties and subjective right-sided weakness; neurologic workup including CT head and CTA head/neck showed no acute findings, with changes attributed to a prior stroke. Her anticoagulation was transitioned from rivaroxaban to therapeutic enoxaparin due to concerns about absorption. Pain was managed with Dilaudid suppositories, and she was discharged home on TPN, G-tube care, and follow-up plans with a new GI surgeon and specialists.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Unspecified severe protein-calorie malnutrition",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Aphasia",
      "Anemia, unspecified",
      "Unspecified viral hepatitis C without hepatic coma",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 23.0-23.9, adult",
      "Acquired absence of other specified parts of digestive tract",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Personal history of other venous thrombosis and embolism"
    ]
  }
}
